    "turn_text": "have the experience of the 2008 Farm Bill. Many of them don't have the experience of the efforts last year, the last two years, the ones who just got elected last November. So both Chairman Lucas and Ranking Member Peterson and I think some of those of us who have been involved in this for five, six years or longer, In my case, this is my ninth year, are trying to explain, you know, the progress that has been made, the fact that we've reduced the amount of total dollars that have been spent on the Farm Bill from the 2008 to the prior 2004 Farm Bill and our efforts last year were going to again be the effort to save additional money and provide changes in areas from the program crops to the conservation areas as well as the dairy tile. And so, I mean, that part involves an education process. And I think it takes Republicans and Democrats working together to indicate where we've been and where we are today and the challenges that we're going to face this year if we're successfully going to produce a farm bill.",
